{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons","id":1021864,"title":"[Viking Dark Era] Why not dragons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T23:48:32-08:00","id":1021864,"title":"[Viking Dark Era] Why not dragons?","content":"So I maybe played too much <b>Skyrim</b>, but I <i>really</i> wanted to add dragons to Viking game I plan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How could make them work in the setting? I suppose that Sea Serpents totem spirits would be typical for ship crews. Some even could make Claimed ( or even one or two left Pangeans ) that are inside gigantic sea snakes. But what about classical, European, fire breathing dragons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T01:52:58-08:00","id":1021902,"title":"","content":"Magath is the obvious answer, as well as idigam. If you want them to be more natural though, spirits of legend could work (not legendary spirits, spirits with influence (legends) who show up as some legendary creature).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T02:49:05-08:00","id":1021910,"title":"","content":"If I remember, there where some 'dragon -like' creature in Sunered World Dark Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:41:19-08:00","id":1021936,"title":"","content":"I would expect those would either be a weird creature that's rather unique and mysterious, or a pangean. I tend to not think much about pangeans though, cause I run with the &quot;they're all dead or gone&quot; idea, except for stuff like hosts, uratha and other shifters of course.<br /> <br /> Edit: I never really read dark eras too heavily myself, except for requiem for regina, so I don't remember much myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6365,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","user":"Fumus","date":". 12-25-2016, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:04:46-08:00","id":1021944,"title":"","content":"By dragons, are you talking about that &quot;classic&quot; typical fire-breathing reptile with wings? Then yeah, spirits and magath and Claimed are the way to go, given how that type of dragons are a mixture of various mythic themes.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can always use the Dread Horror rules in the core to make up a dragon and throw them at players. It's not like werewolves particularly care about where the prey lie in the grand metaphysical scheme. As long as it makes a good hunt, they'll wage the Siskur-Dah on it.<br /> <br /> If we're allowing non-classic dragons, the ones often described as wyverns and serpents nowadays are easier. Spirits of sea, treasure, power, and such. They're closer to natural animals in form, so it's easier to justify their shapes, and besides they're the more &quot;classic&quot; dragons if we track down the origins of dragons anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:22:16-08:00","id":1021949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1021910#post1021910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember, there where some 'dragon -like' creature in Sunered World Dark Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou're probably thinking of the post-chrysalis Idigam in the Babbling Tower story seed of Sundered World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:43:16-08:00","id":1021952,"title":"","content":"Viking dragons seemed more serpent-like than draconic. Lindworms. They would probably fit best as hive-claimed, due to their propensity for eating the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T06:07:02-08:00","id":1021957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1021949#post1021949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYou're probably thinking of the post-chrysalis Idigam in the Babbling Tower story seed of Sundered World.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Idigam is also way to do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More, maybe with Sundered World 'prequel' story to add to chronicle timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T06:52:59-08:00","id":1021970,"title":"","content":"Or even make the 'mook' dragons be spirits and Claimed, with the Alduin equivalent the idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T07:12:06-08:00","id":1021973,"title":"","content":"Or a crossover with Beast the Primordial. There's PC-able dragons there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T08:37:21-08:00","id":1021994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1021973#post1021973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a crossover with Beast the Primordial. There's PC-able dragons there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are not <i>physical </i>12 meters gigantic lizards with wings. They are more like 'ghosts' ( goetia to be precise ) of those great dragons. Idigam or Pangean version are still more in the same gameline territory that we can recreate almost exactly like 'european dragon'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T09:33:56-08:00","id":1022014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1021952#post1021952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Viking dragons seemed more serpent-like than draconic. Lindworms. They would probably fit best as hive-claimed, due to their propensity for eating the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>\u200b</i>\u200bI had a specific idea for a particular type of Hive-Claimed during the Viking era. Might get round to writing all that stuff up one day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T10:32:12-08:00","id":1022032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1021994#post1021994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they are not <i>physical </i>12 meters gigantic lizards with wings. They are more like 'ghosts' ( goetia to be precise ) of those great dragons. Idigam or Pangean version are still more in the same gameline territory that we can recreate almost exactly like 'european dragon'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't Beasts take the form of their Horrors when they impose their Lairs on reality? Or am I misremembering?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T10:44:55-08:00","id":1022036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1022032#post1022032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't Beasts take the form of their Horrors when they impose their Lairs on reality? Or am I misremembering?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed more or less how it goes, and one of the main benefits of Chambers is that they provide direct or indirect access to the biggest dicepool you can swing at opening a Pathway \u2014 and five successes means the overlap lasts for the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:03:28-08:00","id":1022063,"title":"","content":"Oh, they're certainly dragons, can appear as dragons in the physical world, can be kaiju sized if they want. Its just a question if you want to include crossover or not in your game. *Shrugs* Just a suggestion, so take your pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T14:59:03-08:00","id":1022099,"title":"","content":"Crazy thought... Maybe just make dragons a real thing and stat it out. So instead of claimed it's a physical real dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T15:55:44-08:00","id":1022109,"title":"","content":"Presumably wyrdhamster wants it to be something more werewolf-focused, so he asked on the werewolf forum for other ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T21:05:39-08:00","id":1022205,"title":"","content":"i dont see how homebrewing a beast into the world of werewolf makes it any less werewolf then just &quot;the spirits did it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T21:40:30-08:00","id":1022216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1022205#post1022205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i dont see how homebrewing a beast into the world of werewolf makes it any less werewolf then just &quot;the spirits did it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits have a motive, a reason for being, a reason for doing what they do, a bane and ban that's an extension of those reasons. It's a lot more than 'just' 'the spirits did it.'<br /> <br /> And while werewolves can hunt anything, further tying whatever monster you want to make into werewolf usually involves tying it somehow to the spiritual world. There's other ways you can go, of course, like with shartha or idigam or Pangaean or Pangaean relics. But if you have a pack that's heavily focused on spirit shamanism, they're not going to have much incentive to go after a random beast. It's there, it's been doing its thing, who cares. Alternatively tying things into the spirit is a way to guarantee some extra 'features' to a spirit-borne threat. Wiping out a powerful spirit that's Reached across is going to cause a vacuum on the other side of the Gauntlet, which allows for more plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Plus against individual monsters, werewolves are pretty dominant and a pack would likely annihilate a homebrewed dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:09:21-08:00","id":1024944,"title":"","content":"For Old Norse dragons, remember this:<br /> 1) They are mostly giant snakes, not winged lizards. They can generally fly though.<br /> 2) They aren't fire-breathers, they are instead poisonous/acidic.<br /> 3) They are generally thematically connected with water, the deep, and caves. (Riches of the deep, and all that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:39:53-08:00","id":1024966,"title":"","content":"Don't they eat corpses, too?<br /> <br /> I remember trying to work out something where Snake, the last of the Pangaeans, was found in Ireland by some Vikings, including a werewolf going through their First Change. So I ended up looking into the linnorms and Nastrond and Nidhoggr. Then got sidetracked by ideas about the giants so I looked into them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-31-2016, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T17:39:33-08:00","id":1025208,"title":"","content":"Nidhogg eats corpses but that isn't a sign of all dragons, just the one from below the tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T18:35:39-08:00","id":1025228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1025208#post1025208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nidhogg eats corpses but that isn't a sign of all dragons, just the one from below the tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only a few, and two of them eat corpses, as Jormungand also eats the dead. What else do they eat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T19:20:46-08:00","id":1025237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1025228#post1025228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's only a few, and two of them eat corpses, as Jormungand also eats the dead. What else do they eat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not seen anything of jormungandr eating the dead. I've seen him eating Thor, but he just exists in the ocean. Clearly has a taste for cattle aswell. There are lindworms in fairy tales that eat people iirc. Fafnir just became a dragon out of greed, and his helm was what generated all the terror. Of what I've read though nidhogg is specifically for eating the dead.<br /> <br /> As an aside the Ragnarok event is likely heavily Christian influenced (as everyone brings up) so nidhogg gnawing corpses may be something added to bring the idea of hel as a bad place to the fore. From what I can gather Norse hel is closer to Greek hadies. <br /> <br /> That said, Ragnarok is the most metal story ever told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T20:25:54-08:00","id":1025260,"title":"","content":"When fishing for Jormungandr they used an ox's severed head. And body. Since the former worked it stands to reason it won't run away from eating the dead. I think Seidmedr is our resident Norse expert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-01-2017, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:26:22-08:00","id":1026018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1025260#post1025260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When fishing for Jormungandr they used an ox's severed head. And body. Since the former worked it stands to reason it won't run away from eating the dead. I think Seidmedr is our resident Norse expert.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you think that way of me, but I'm in no way an expert, just an overly enthusiastic amateur, who is wrong as often as not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But as to the midgard serpent? I think it's just a meat eater in general, rather than specifically a corpse-gnawer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:37:35-08:00","id":1026032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1026018#post1026018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad you think that way of me, but I'm in no way an expert, just an overly enthusiastic amateur, who is wrong as often as not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>-ArcaneArts on Changeling, 2012","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:35:20-08:00","id":1026079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1026018#post1026018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad you think that way of me, but I'm in no way an expert, just an overly enthusiastic amateur, who is wrong as often as not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But as to the midgard serpent? I think it's just a meat eater in general, rather than specifically a corpse-gnawer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly not sure I'd qualify the midgard serpent as a dragon either, he seems more a giant snake then a dragon. &gt;.&gt; though if i were being technical I might say giant kin in the form of a snake. The eater of the moon is referred to in one passage as a troll in the shape of a wolf. But then snorri bounces around a bit on nomenclature and its hard to be sure what's a kenning versus a name. The same could be said of fafnir, whom we know as a dwarf, but according to Hollander's translation of the poetic edda, in the original mythos Fafnir and his family were of the giant race, not dwarven. <br /> <br /> A dragon or two appear in the fairy tales &quot;east of the sun west of the moon&quot; collection, called lindworms, but thats a more modern set of tales then those of the viking age so its hard to say. I suppose dragons in the beowulf epic might be best to look at as a general archetype, or we could just ignore all of what i've said at large and take them all as dragons of various types. Doing a quick flip through my copy of beowulf (this one also has the old english version so its pretty nifty) has a fire dragon, which does breath flames. Jormungandr being poisonous might be due more to his serpentine quality then draconic.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.theparisreview.org/blog/2015/05/22/the-lindworm/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theparisreview.org/blog/.../the-lindworm/</a> here is a nice review of the lindworm prine. While you could limit them all to being spirits, I find it a shame and would rather see dragons as dragons proper. I haven't read beast yet so i've no clue how that gameline handles them. If you'd want to go the spirit route with them I'd make it a full court with a penchant towards lineage, as most things in nordic history are seemingly obsessed with proving family ancestry. <br /> <br /> Another option would be to dig up the conversion rules for fera from werewolf the apocalypse to forsaken (granted its a first edition conversion, but the stats should remain roughly the same) and convert over a mokole of your choosing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:56:17-08:00","id":1026637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons#post1021864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I maybe played too much <b>Skyrim</b>, but I <i>really</i> wanted to add dragons to Viking game I plan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How could make them work in the setting? I suppose that Sea Serpents totem spirits would be typical for ship crews. Some even could make Claimed ( or even one or two left Pangeans ) that are inside gigantic sea snakes. But what about classical, European, fire breathing dragons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Horrors from Chronicles of Darkness seems like an obvious answer, but I don't see it posted yet. I'd feel free to pick and choose Dread Powers sources as appropriate and make.<br /> <br /> <br /> Potency 7,<br /> Dread Powers: Unbreakable, Immortal, Numen-Blast, Colossus (WtF2ed) Numen- Seek (Greed), Influence 1 (Greed)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-04-2017, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:10:01-08:00","id":1026645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1026079#post1026079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly not sure I'd qualify the midgard serpent as a dragon either, he seems more a giant snake then a dragon. &gt;.&gt; though if i were being technical I might say giant kin in the form of a snake. The eater of the moon is referred to in one passage as a troll in the shape of a wolf. But then snorri bounces around a bit on nomenclature and its hard to be sure what's a kenning versus a name. The same could be said of fafnir, whom we know as a dwarf, but according to Hollander's translation of the poetic edda, in the original mythos Fafnir and his family were of the giant race, not dwarven.<br /> <br /> A dragon or two appear in the fairy tales &quot;east of the sun west of the moon&quot; collection, called lindworms, but thats a more modern set of tales then those of the viking age so its hard to say. I suppose dragons in the beowulf epic might be best to look at as a general archetype, or we could just ignore all of what i've said at large and take them all as dragons of various types. Doing a quick flip through my copy of beowulf (this one also has the old english version so its pretty nifty) has a fire dragon, which does breath flames. Jormungandr being poisonous might be due more to his serpentine quality then draconic.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.theparisreview.org/blog/2015/05/22/the-lindworm/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theparisreview.org/blog/.../the-lindworm/</a> here is a nice review of the lindworm prine. While you could limit them all to being spirits, I find it a shame and would rather see dragons as dragons proper. I haven't read beast yet so i've no clue how that gameline handles them. If you'd want to go the spirit route with them I'd make it a full court with a penchant towards lineage, as most things in nordic history are seemingly obsessed with proving family ancestry.<br /> <br /> Another option would be to dig up the conversion rules for fera from werewolf the apocalypse to forsaken (granted its a first edition conversion, but the stats should remain roughly the same) and convert over a mokole of your choosing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The definition of a dragon is a bit complicated.<br /> As far as I get it, the regular term was just orm (cognate with worm/wyrm), which is also the term for snake.<br /> So when someone calls someone a wormtongue, in an old Norse context, they are also calling them dragon-tongued and snake-tongued. And that's an insult with a compliment baked in. Kinda cool.<br /> (Oh, and lindorm just means coiling snake. That specific combinations of words isn't used in modern Swedish, but that's what the meaning of the words is.)<br /> <br /> I'm pretty certain the fire breathing dragons came with continental influence, since, you know, giant evil reptile myths seem pretty interchangeable after all, right? Especially since both had an &quot;and my breath is death&quot;-thing going on. Both poison and fire will kill you up, after all.<br /> Beowulf as we know it today was written down in what today is England, a land which has had quite a lot of continental influences (especially compared to Scandinavia at the time).<br /> <br /> But as to a Werewolf context?<br /> I'd probably try to tie the weird-ass snake hosts into it somehow. Talking about their dead father-god who once encircled the world. But now each of them carry a shard of his heart in theirs...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1026032#post1026032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-ArcaneArts on Changeling, 2012</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll keep that in mind if OPP ever does Viking: the Sea-faring. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:19:26-08:00","id":1026649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021864-viking-dark-era-why-not-dragons?p=1026645#post1026645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll keep that in mind if OPP ever does Viking: the Sea-faring. <img src=\"h